{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nitro-zombie-mealworm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nREVIEW_RESULT sidecars are keyed `(change_id, revision)` (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py:38-58`). A finding that the reviewer emits on one patchset and does not repeat on the next simply disappears: on Gerrit change 1867 the advisory naming the exact defect (`tapestried-abhorrent-tuna`) appeared on patchsets 1–2, was absent on 3–4, and the change merged unchanged. Recall per run is non-deterministic, so a finding's lifetime is currently one revision. Approved in the fortnight defect review (2026-08-21).\n\n## Approach\nWhen `finalize.py` assembles a review for revision N, load revision N-1's sidecar (same `change_id`), take its findings whose disposition is neither `addressed` nor `withdrawn`, and hand them to the Pass-2 verifier as standing items against the new diff. The verifier records each as `still-present`, `addressed` (diff changed the cited lines and the condition no longer holds), or `withdrawn` (re-grounding fails). Standing items keep their criterion and posture — an advisory stays advisory — so no new blocks arise from carry-forward alone. Persist the disposition in the new sidecar so the chain is auditable.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py`, `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py`, `src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py`, `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-verifier.md` (standing-item instructions), `src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py` (publish carried findings with their origin revision), `tests/unit/llm/code_review/test_finding_carry_forward.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: a finding on revision 1 not re-emitted on revision 2 is presented to the verifier and recorded `still-present`. Edge: the cited lines are deleted on revision 2 → `addressed`; revision 1 has no sidecar (first review) → no standing items; a rebase-only revision keeps all items. Pinning: `tests/unit/llm/code_review/test_sidecar*.py`, `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A finding present on revision N-1 and absent from the fresh Pass-1 output on revision N appears in revision N's sidecar with a disposition; checked by the new unit test.\n- [ ] Carry-forward never raises a finding's posture; checked by a test asserting blocking/advisory is unchanged across revisions.\n- [ ] Gerrit messages show carried findings with \"since patchset k\"; checked by the review-bot adapter test.\n","id":"7f54-9ef2-356a-4551","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","priority":2,"tags":["gates","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Carry unresolved code-review findings forward across patchsets"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787354707836151001,"uuid":"78b5857c-ed2b-4251-98f1-a3253a087b1e"}